al feeding on the short-term outcomes of patients undergoing laparoscopic distal gastrectomy. In addition to this work, Yang J is also a researcher engaged in studies that explore the impact of dietary factors on cancer risk.", "BMC CANCER:BMC Cancer is a peer-reviewed medical journal dedicated to publishing research articles related to cancer. It encompasses a wide range of topics, including meta-analyses, systematic reviews, and studies focusing on nutritional outcomes in cancer patients. Notably, BMC Cancer has also published the study protocol for the PROPILS trial, further contributing to the body of research in the field of oncology.", "AMERICAN JOURNAL OF CLINICAL NUTRITION:The \"American Journal of Clinical Nutrition\" is a leading, peer-reviewed journal dedicated to publishing original research and reviews in the field of clinical nutrition. It focuses on the effects of nutrition on health and disease, encompassing a wide range of topics including obesity, dietary intake, and various health outcomes. The journal features studies related to specific dietary components, such as dairy consumption, dietary fat intake, calcium, phosphorus, and copper metabolism, as well as their implications for disease risk, including cancer and heart disease.\n\nThe American Journal of Clinical Nutrition serves as a vital resource for researchers and practitioners in the field of nutrition and dietetics, providing insights into the dietary management of conditions like phenylketonuria and metabolic disorders. By publishing research on the impact of nutrition on health, the journal contributes significantly to the understanding of how dietary choices influence overall well-being and the prevention of chronic diseases.", "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF CLINICAL PRACTICE:The International Journal of Clinical Practice is a peer-reviewed journal dedicated to publishing research on clinical practices and guidelines in the field of medicine. It focuses on various aspects of clinical research and practice, including studies related to cancer risk and dietary factors. The journal serves as a platform for disseminating important findings that can influence clinical practices and improve patient care.", "NUTRITION CANCER:Nutrition Cancer is a journal dedicated to exploring the intricate relationship between nutrition and cancer. It publishes a wide range of research, including studies that examine the impact of dietary factors, such as dairy products, on cancer risk. The journal also focuses on dietary interventions specifically designed for cancer patients, providing insights into how nutrition can influence cancer outcomes. Additionally, Nutrition Cancer features meta-analyses that synthesize existing research on dietary factors and their association with cancer risk, contributing to a deeper understanding of how nutrition can affect cancer prevention and management.", "EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF CLINICAL NUTRITION:The European Journal of Clinical Nutrition (Eur J Clin Nutr) is a peer-reviewed journal dedicated to publishing research on various aspects of nutrition and its impact on health. It covers a wide range of topics, including inter-observer variability in body composition measurement, cancer risk studies, and the implications of clinical nutrition for health and disease. The journal also focuses on specific issues such as sarcopenia and its effects on the elderly, as well as studies and guidelines related to the management of eating disorders. Through its comprehensive research publications, the European Journal of Clinical Nutrition aims to advance the understanding of nutrition and its critical role in health outcomes."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}